# Engagement runtime data - per-target state, evidence, and findings never ship.
# The TEMPLATE ships so the layout stays documented and git-tracked.
#
# Ignore by *file pattern at depth*, not by ignoring the directory. A blanket
# 'engagements/*' excludes each target directory itself, and git never descends
# into an excluded directory - so '!engagements/TEMPLATE' could not re-include
# anything, and a newly created engagement's files were silently uncommittable.
# Only files already in the index survived, which hid the breakage until the next
# new engagement. Same protection, without the trap.
engagements/*/findings.json
engagements/*/findings.csv
engagements/*/candidates.json
engagements/*/results.json
engagements/*/results.csv
engagements/*/chain.json
engagements/*/state.json.lock
engagements/**/evidence/
engagements/**/report.md
engagements/**/recon.json
engagements/**/.lock
# Re-include the shipped template last, so the rules above cannot re-ignore it.
!engagements/TEMPLATE/state.json
!engagements/TEMPLATE/findings/findings.csv

# Engagement/scan artifacts that can carry target data or credentials
*_results.json
api_scan_*.json
secret_scan_*.txt
dorks_*.json
cve-feed.json

# Backups
*.bak
*.bakup
*.backup
*.old
